    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4298",
      "problem": "Let $A(1,3)$ and $B(2,-2).$ Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252505/assets/f95ee3c5c81750d97019d910350e4c78f0962baa682c834928450a451691145a.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=i+3j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=2i-2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-2j)-(i+3j) \\\\  & =i-5j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{26}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
